{"tool_name":"basic","contents":["biocontainers","biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:basic"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"basic","identifiers":["biotools:basic","doi:10.1038/ncomms14836"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Basic is a semi-de novo assembly method for assembling bcr and tcr genes  from single cell rna-seq data.","home_url":"https://github.com/akds/BASIC","keywords":["Artifacts","Image Processing, Computer-Assisted","Microscopy","Time-Lapse Imaging","Biological imaging","Imaging","Biomarkers","RNA-Seq"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"basic","home":"http://sites.imagej.net/BaSiC/","summary":"Background and shading correction of optical microscopy images.","addition_date":"2018-07-08T12:40:14Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:32:11.602457Z","tool_type":["Plug-in"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:basic","credit":[{"email":"carsten.marr@helmholtz-muenchen.de","name":"Carsten Marr","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www.helmholtz-muenchen.de/icb/research/groups/quantitative-single-cell-dynamics/software/basic/index.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"}]}],"name":"BaSiC","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms14836","metadata":{"abstract":"Quantitative analysis of bioimaging data is often skewed by both shading in space and background variation in time. We introduce BaSiC, an image correction method based on low-rank and sparse decomposition which solves both issues. In comparison to existing shading correction tools, BaSiC achieves high-accuracy with significantly fewer input images, works for diverse imaging conditions and is robust against artefacts. Moreover, it can correct temporal drift in time-lapse microscopy data and thus improve continuous single-cell quantification. Ba